# Public frontend configuration; never put secrets in VITE_ variables.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
# Provider settings are Worker vars in worker/wrangler.jsonc:
# OVERPASS_URL, NOMINATIM_URL, OSRM_URL_TEMPLATE, PROVIDER_USER_AGENT, TILE_URL, ALLOWED_ORIGIN.
# Local D1 migrations run via npm run dev. Remote deployment needs a real D1 database ID.
# Worker secrets belong in worker/.dev.vars or wrangler secret put NAME.

# OPEN_METEO_URL: free non-commercial forecast endpoint; see README for limits.
# Worker secret ADMIN_TOKEN: long random operator token, worker/.dev.vars locally; wrangler secret put ADMIN_TOKEN for deployment.
# WIKIDATA_URL=https://query.wikidata.org/sparql (Worker var; official free CC0 open-data API).
# WIKIDATA_USER_AGENT=SPOTLAND/0.1 (YOUR_PUBLIC_PROJECT_URL_OR_CONTACT_EMAIL)
# Set a real public operator contact in worker/.dev.vars or Worker vars; left unset so live fetching is disabled.

# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=123-YOUR_PUBLIC_WEB_CLIENT.apps.googleusercontent.com
# Worker var only (or worker/.dev.vars locally). Public OAuth client ID, not an API key/client secret.
# GOOGLE_JWKS_URL=https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v3/certs (only this official endpoint is accepted).
# Accounts require VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api and the same-origin Pages API service binding.
# DEVICE_SECRET: at least 32 random bytes encoded as base64url (43+ characters).
# Worker secret only: worker/.dev.vars locally; wrangler secret put DEVICE_SECRET for deployment.
# Sharing requires the same-origin /api proxy and HTTPS (or supported secure localhost).

# SOS_ENABLED=true (Worker var; enables the no-login SOS/nearby API after migration 0007).
# PUSH_ENABLED=true enables receiving/private push tests with configured keys while SOS_ENABLED=false keeps broadcast sending paused.
# Optional Web Push: VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, VAPID_SUBJECT (approved mailto contact or HTTPS operator URL).
# Generate/preserve local keys with: node scripts/setup-push.mjs --subject YOUR_APPROVED_PUBLIC_CONTACT
# Keys are saved only in git-ignored worker/.dev.vars. Never expose the private key in VITE_ config.
# Production requires the same key pair in Worker secrets, production D1 and HTTPS service-worker setup.

# M6 uses existing D1, ALLOWED_ORIGIN, OSRM_URL_TEMPLATE and OPEN_METEO_URL.
# Apply 0008_trips.sql remotely before deployment; no new provider key is needed.
